# 4. Behavioral Patterns

Behavioral patterns are concerned with algorithms and the assignment of responsibilities between objects. The Online Book Store implements two behavioral patterns: **Strategy** and **Observer**.

---

## 4.1 Strategy Pattern

### Purpose

Define a family of algorithms, encapsulate each one, and make them interchangeable. Strategy pattern lets the algorithm vary independently from clients that use it.

### Problem Statement

Books can be sorted in multiple ways:
- By price (low to high, high to low)
- By popularity 
- By title (A-Z, Z-A)

Without the Strategy pattern, the BookService would need:
- Hard-coded sorting logic with conditional statements
- Modification every time a new sorting method is added
- Violates Open/Closed Principle

### Implementation

The Strategy pattern is implemented with 1 interface and 5 concrete strategies.

#### 4.1.1 Strategy Interface

**Location**: [Models/SortStrategy.java](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/SortStrategy.java)

```java
package com.example.onlinebookstore.Models;

import java.util.List;

/**
 * Strategy Pattern Interface:
 * Defines the contract for all sorting strategies.
 */
public interface SortStrategy {
    void sort(List<Book> books);
}
```

#### 4.1.2 Concrete Strategies

**1. SortByPrice** (Low to High)

**Location**: [Models/SortByPrice.java](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/SortByPrice.java)

```java
package com.example.onlinebookstore.Models;

import java.util.Comparator;
import java.util.List;

/**
 * Concrete Strategy: Sorts by price, low to high.
 */
public class SortByPrice implements SortStrategy {
    @Override
    public void sort(List<Book> books) {
        books.sort(Comparator.comparingDouble(Book::getPrice));
    }
}
```

**2. SortByPriceHighToLow**

**Location**: [Models/SortByPriceHighToLow.java](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/SortByPriceHighToLow.java)

```java
package com.example.onlinebookstore.Models;

import java.util.Comparator;
import java.util.List;

public class SortByPriceHighToLow implements SortStrategy {
    @Override
    public void sort(List<Book> books) {
        books.sort(Comparator.comparingDouble(Book::getPrice).reversed());
    }
}
```

**3. SortByPopularity**

**Location**: [Models/SortByPopularity.java](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/SortByPopularity.java)

```java
package com.example.onlinebookstore.Models;

import java.util.Comparator;
import java.util.List;

public class SortByPopularity implements SortStrategy {
    @Override
    public void sort(List<Book> books) {
        books.sort(Comparator.comparingInt(Book::getPopularity).reversed());
    }
}
```

**4. SortByTitleAZ**

**Location**: [Models/SortByTitleAZ.java](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/SortByTitleAZ.java)

```java
package com.example.onlinebookstore.Models;

import java.util.Comparator;
import java.util.List;

public class SortByTitleAZ implements SortStrategy {
    @Override
    public void sort(List<Book> books) {
        books.sort(Comparator.comparing(Book::getTitle));
    }
}
```

**5. SortByTitleZA**

**Location**: [Models/SortByTitleZA.java](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/SortByTitleZA.java)

```java
package com.example.onlinebookstore.Models;

import java.util.Comparator;
import java.util.List;

public class SortByTitleZA implements SortStrategy {
    @Override
    public void sort(List<Book> books) {
        books.sort(Comparator.comparing(Book::getTitle).reversed());
    }
}
```

### Strategy Pattern Structure

```
           SortStrategy (Interface)
                    │
                    │ implements
     ┌──────────────┼──────────────┬─────────────┬─────────────┐
     │              │              │             │             │
SortByPrice  SortByPriceH2L  SortByPopularity  SortByTitleAZ  SortByTitleZA
```

#### 4.1.3 Context Class (BookService)

**Location**: [Models/BookService.java](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/BookService.java)

```java
package com.example.onlinebookstore.Models;

import java.util.List;

/**
 * Service for book-related logic.
 * Uses the Strategy pattern for sorting.
 */
public class BookService {
    private BookDAO bookDAO;

    public BookService() {
        this.bookDAO = new BookDAO();
    }

    public List<Book> getBooks(SortStrategy sortStrategy) {
        List<Book> books = bookDAO.getAllBooks();
        // Apply the chosen strategy
        if (sortStrategy != null) {
            sortStrategy.sort(books);
        }
        return books;
    }
}
```

### Usage in BookStoreFacade

```java
public class BookStoreFacade {
    private BookService bookService;
    
    public List<Book> getAllBooks() {
        return bookService.getBooks(null); // No sorting
    }
    
    public List<Book> getBooksSortedByPrice() {
        return bookService.getBooks(new SortByPrice());
    }
    
    public List<Book> getBooksSortedByPopularity() {
        return bookService.getBooks(new SortByPopularity());
    }
}
```

### Usage in Controllers

```java
public class CustomerDashboardController {
    private BookStoreFacade facade;
    
    public void handleSortByPrice() {
        List<Book> books = facade.getBooksSortedByPrice();
        displayBooks(books);
    }
    
    public void handleSortByPopularity() {
        List<Book> books = facade.getBooksSortedByPopularity();
        displayBooks(books);
    }
    
    public void handleSortByTitle() {
        List<Book> books = facade.getAllBooks(); // Get all first
        new SortByTitleAZ().sort(books); // Apply strategy
        displayBooks(books);
    }
}
```

### Strategy Pattern Benefits

| Benefit | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| **Open/Closed Principle** | Open for extension (new strategies), closed for modification |
| **Runtime Selection** | Strategy can be chosen dynamically at runtime |
| **No Conditional Logic** | Eliminates if-else chains for different sorting approaches |
| **Easy to Extend** | Add new sorting strategies without modifying existing code |
| **Testable** | Each strategy can be tested independently |
| **Reusable** | Strategies can be reused across different contexts |

### Adding a New Strategy

To add a new sorting strategy (e.g., by author name):

```java
public class SortByAuthor implements SortStrategy {
    @Override
    public void sort(List<Book> books) {
        books.sort(Comparator.comparing(Book::getAuthor));
    }
}

// Usage in Facade
public List<Book> getBooksSortedByAuthor() {
    return bookService.getBooks(new SortByAuthor());
}
```

**No changes required** to:
- [SortStrategy](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/SortStrategy.java#9-12) interface
- Existing strategies
- [BookService](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/BookService.java#9-27) class
- Any other part of the system

### Strategy Pattern Flow

```
1. User clicks "Sort by Price"
        ↓
2. Controller calls facade.getBooksSortedByPrice()
        ↓
3. Facade creates new SortByPrice() strategy
        ↓
4. Facade calls bookService.getBooks(strategy)
        ↓
5. BookService retrieves books from BookDAO
        ↓
6. BookService calls strategy.sort(books)
        ↓
7. SortByPrice applies comparator to sort list
        ↓
8. Sorted books returned to Controller
        ↓
9. Controller displays sorted books
```

**[PLACEHOLDER: Strategy Pattern Class Diagram]**

### All Available Strategies

| Strategy | Sorting Criterion | Order |
|----------|-------------------|-------|
| [SortByPrice](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/SortByPrice.java#10-16) | Price | Low → High |
| `SortByPriceHighToLow` | Price | High → Low |
| `SortByPopularity` | Popularity (sales count) | High → Low |
| `SortByTitleAZ` | Title (alphabetically) | A → Z |
| `SortByTitleZA` | Title (alphabetically) | Z → A |

