## 4.2 Observer Pattern

### Purpose

Define a one-to-many dependency between objects so that when one object changes state, all its dependents are notified and updated automatically.

### Problem Statement

**Scenario**: When an admin confirms an order, the inventory must be updated automatically by reducing stock for each ordered book.

**Without Observer**:
- [OrderService](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/OrderService.java#11-134) would need to directly call [InventoryService](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/InventoryService.java#9-46)
- Tight coupling between services
- Hard to add more reactions to order events (e.g., email notifications, analytics)

**With Observer**:
- [OrderService](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/OrderService.java#11-134) doesn't know about [InventoryService](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/InventoryService.java#9-46)
- Loose coupling via Observer interface
- Easy to add more observers

### Implementation

The Observer pattern involves:
- **Subject Interface**: `OrderSubject`
- **Observer Interface**: [OrderObserver](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/OrderObserver.java#5-13)
- **Concrete Subject**: [OrderService](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/OrderService.java#11-134)
- **Concrete Observer**: [InventoryService](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/InventoryService.java#9-46)

#### 4.2.1 Observer Interface

**Location**: [Models/OrderObserver.java](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/OrderObserver.java)

```java
package com.example.onlinebookstore.Models;

import java.util.List;

public interface OrderObserver {
    void onOrderConfirmed(Order order);
    
    // New method with order items for proper stock updates
    default void onOrderConfirmed(Order order, List<OrderItem> items) {
        onOrderConfirmed(order); // Default to legacy behavior
    }
}
```

#### 4.2.2 Subject Interface

**Location**: [Models/OrderSubject.java](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/OrderSubject.java)

```java
package com.example.onlinebookstore.Models;

public interface OrderSubject {
    void addObserver(OrderObserver observer);
    void removeObserver(OrderObserver observer);
    void notifyObservers(Order order);
}
```

#### 4.2.3 Concrete Subject (OrderService)

**Location**: [Models/OrderService.java](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/OrderService.java)

```java
package com.example.onlinebookstore.Models;

import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

/**
 * Service for order logic.
 * Implements Subject for the Observer pattern.
 */
public class OrderService implements OrderSubject {
    private OrderDAO orderDAO;
    private OrderItemDAO orderItemDAO;
    private List<OrderObserver> observers = new ArrayList<>();

    public OrderService() {
        this.orderDAO = new OrderDAO();
        this.orderItemDAO = new OrderItemDAO();
    }

    public boolean confirmOrder(Order order) {
        // 1. Validate stock availability for all items
        List<OrderItem> items = orderItemDAO.getOrderItemsByOrder(order.getId());
        BookDAO bookDAO = new BookDAO();
        
        for (OrderItem item : items) {
            Book book = bookDAO.getBookByID(item.getBookId());
            if (book == null || book.getStock() < item.getQuantity()) {
                System.out.println("Cannot confirm order - insufficient stock");
                return false;
            }
        }
        
        // 2. Update order status to 'CONFIRMED'
        order.setStatus("CONFIRMED");
        orderDAO.updateOrderStatus(order.getId(), "CONFIRMED");

        // 3. Notify all observers (e.g., InventoryService)
        notifyObservers(order, items);
        
        return true;
    }
    
    // Overloaded method with items
    public void notifyObservers(Order order, List<OrderItem> items) {
        for (OrderObserver observer : observers) {
            observer.onOrderConfirmed(order, items);
        }
    }

    @Override
    public void addObserver(OrderObserver observer) {
        observers.add(observer);
    }

    @Override
    public void removeObserver(OrderObserver observer) {
        observers.remove(observer);
    }

    @Override
    public void notifyObservers(Order order) {
        for (OrderObserver observer : observers) {
            observer.onOrderConfirmed(order);
        }
    }
}
```

#### 4.2.4 Concrete Observer (InventoryService)

**Location**: [Models/InventoryService.java](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/InventoryService.java)

```java
package com.example.onlinebookstore.Models;

import java.util.List;

/**
 * Observer Implementation:
 * Listens for order confirmations to update stock.
 */
public class InventoryService implements OrderObserver {
    private BookDAO bookDAO;

    public InventoryService() {
        this.bookDAO = new BookDAO();
    }

    @Override
    public void onOrderConfirmed(Order order) {
        // Legacy method
        System.out.println("InventoryService: Order " + order.getId() + " confirmed");
    }
    
    @Override
    public void onOrderConfirmed(Order order, List<OrderItem> items) {
        System.out.println("InventoryService: Order " + order.getId() + 
                           " confirmed. Updating stock...");

        // Update stock for each item in the order
        for (OrderItem item : items) {
            Book book = bookDAO.getBookByID(item.getBookId());
            if (book != null) {
                int newStock = book.getStock() - item.getQuantity();
                if (newStock < 0) newStock = 0; // Safety check
                bookDAO.updateBookStock(item.getBookId(), newStock);
                System.out.println("Updated stock for book ID " + item.getBookId() + 
                                   " (qty: " + item.getQuantity() + ") to " + newStock);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

### Observer Registration

Observers are registered in the [BookStoreFacade](file:///c:/Users/Ahmed/IdeaProjects/Online-Book-Store/src/main/java/com/example/onlinebookstore/Models/BookStoreFacade.java#12-331) constructor:

```java
public class BookStoreFacade {
    private OrderService orderService;
    private InventoryService inventoryService;
    
    public BookStoreFacade() {
        this.orderService = new OrderService();
        this.inventoryService = new InventoryService();
        
        // Wire up the Observer pattern
        this.orderService.addObserver(inventoryService);
    }
}
```

### Observer Pattern Workflow

```
1. Admin views pending orders in AdminDashboard
        ↓
2. Admin clicks "Confirm Order" button
        ↓
3. Controller calls facade.confirmOrder(order)
        ↓
4. Facade calls orderService.confirmOrder(order)
        ↓
5. OrderService validates stock availability
        ↓
6. OrderService updates order status to "CONFIRMED"
        ↓
7. OrderService calls notifyObservers(order, items)
        ↓
8. InventoryService.onOrderConfirmed() is triggered
        ↓
9. InventoryService reduces stock for each book
        ↓
10. BookDAO.updateBookStock() persists changes
        ↓
11. Success message displayed to admin
```

**[PLACEHOLDER: Observer Pattern Sequence Diagram]**

### Observer Pattern Benefits

| Benefit | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| **Loose Coupling** | OrderService doesn't know about InventoryService |
| **Open/Closed** | Easy to add new observers without modifying OrderService |
| **Broadcast** | Multiple observers can react to the same event |
| **Separation of Concerns** | Order logic separated from inventory logic |
| **Extensible** | Can add email, analytics, notification observers |

### Potential Additional Observers

The Observer pattern makes it easy to add more reactions to order confirmation:

**1. Email Notification Observer**:
```java
public class EmailNotificationService implements OrderObserver {
    @Override
    public void onOrderConfirmed(Order order, List<OrderItem> items) {
        String customerEmail = getCustomerEmail(order.getCustomerId());
        sendEmail(customerEmail, "Order Confirmed", orderDetails);
    }
}
```

**2. Analytics Observer**:
```java
public class AnalyticsService implements OrderObserver {
    @Override
    public void onOrderConfirmed(Order order, List<OrderItem> items) {
        updateSalesStatistics(order);
        updatePopularityMetrics(items);
    }
}
```

**3. Low Stock Alert Observer**:
```java
public class LowStockAlertService implements OrderObserver {
    @Override
    public void onOrderConfirmed(Order order, List<OrderItem> items) {
        for (OrderItem item : items) {
            Book book = bookDAO.getBookByID(item.getBookId());
            if (book.getStock() < LOW_STOCK_THRESHOLD) {
                alertAdmin("Low stock for: " + book.getTitle());
            }
        }
    }
}
```

**Registration**:
```java
public BookStoreFacade() {
    // existing observers
    this.orderService.addObserver(inventoryService);
    
    // Add new observers
    this.orderService.addObserver(new EmailNotificationService());
    this.orderService.addObserver(new AnalyticsService());
    this.orderService.addObserver(new LowStockAlertService());
}
```

### Observer vs Direct Call

**Direct Call (Tightly Coupled)**:
```java
public boolean confirmOrder(Order order) {
    order.setStatus("CONFIRMED");
    orderDAO.updateOrderStatus(order.getId(), "CONFIRMED");
    
    // Direct dependency - tight coupling
    inventoryService.updateStock(order);
    
    return true;
}
```

**Observer Pattern (Loosely Coupled)**:
```java
public boolean confirmOrder(Order order) {
    order.setStatus("CONFIRMED");
    orderDAO.updateOrderStatus(order.getId(), "CONFIRMED");
    
    // Notify observers - loose coupling
    notifyObservers(order, items);
    
    return true;
}
```

